💬 Viva Questions (with Answers)
Question	Answer
What is a smart contract?	A program stored on a blockchain that executes automatically when conditions are met.
Which language is used to write smart contracts on Ethereum?	Solidity.
What is msg.sender?	The address of the account calling the function.
Why use payable keyword?	To allow the contract to receive or send Ether.
What is the difference between view and pure functions?	view can read state variables, pure cannot read or modify them.
What is a test network?	A blockchain network for testing smart contracts without real Ether.
What is require() used for?	To validate input and ensure conditions before proceeding.
What is the use of mapping?	To store key-value pairs, e.g., user address → balance.
Why is blockchain secure?	Because it is decentralized and uses cryptographic hashing for immutability.
What is gas in Ethereum?	The fee required to execute operations on the Ethereum network.
